SUMMARY:shut in 10.5 mile cardio hike
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nmeet/ park at the river park\nWE H
 IKE AT A FAST PACE WITHOUT BREAKS. This is primarily a fitness oriented ev
 ent. While we try to stay together as a group\, we will not wait for exten
 ded periods at intersections. Sometimes a bit of trail running can even be
  involved. If you haven't hiked with this fitness group before and are uns
 ure of your abilities\, be prepared and know your way back to your car. If
  carpooling is involved please do so appropriately\, or drive yourself to 
 the trailhead.\n\nHIKE DESCRIPTION:\n\nDogs Welcome. The hike is an out & 
 back 10.5 mile LEVEL 7\\* fitness hike that begins at the Bent Creek river
  park where we take a short connector trail to the MST (Mountain to Sea Tr
 ail) South\, to the Sleepy Gap overlook\, and back. The out hike has 3 ste
 ep climbs and for those who desire an additional climbing challenge\, a sp
 ur trail of 400+ feet elevation is available that rejoins the regular MST 
 trail at Sleepy Gap. The return has one steep climb with mild elevation ch
 anges between the 3 steeper downhill sections. The trail parallels the Blu
 e Ridge Parkway and includes an overlook of the French Broad River valley 
 and opposing mountains\, distant views of Asheville. Bring water and snack
 s - we will stop at the turnaround point for a short break so Osa can have
  a snack (or three).
